Small amines such as $\mathrm{NH}_3 \cdot \mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{NH}_2$ and $\left(\mathrm{CH}_3\right)_2 \mathrm{NH}$ give unsymmetrical cleavage of diborane according to following reaction,
$$
\begin{aligned}
&amp; \mathrm{B}_2 \mathrm{H}_6+2 \mathrm{NH}_3 \longrightarrow \\
&amp; {\left[\mathrm{H}_2 \mathrm{~B}\left(\mathrm{NH}_3\right)_2\right]^{+}\left[\mathrm{BH}_4\right]^{-}} \\
&amp;
\end{aligned}
$$
